# Pluto notebooks (Styx)

**Bootstrap only when the user requests notebook work.**

## Skills

- **styx-setup** — install, Julia prerequisite, MCP troubleshooting (before notebook work)
- **pluto-session** — start Pluto, open notebook, Glass navigation
- **pluto-workflow** — cell edits once a notebook is open
- **pluto-semantics** — cell structure (`imports_cell`, `begin`/`end` blocks, `@bind`) and parse-error fixes

Never ask the user to run `pluto-serve.sh` or `PlutoMCP.serve()`. Call `start_pluto_session` / `open_notebook` **by name** even if not in the MCP tool picker. **Glass URL:** local → `pluto_session_status.pluto_url` (no ask); Remote SSH → ask once per session for the Ports forwarded/local port for remote `pluto_port`, then `http://127.0.0.1:<forwarded>/`. Never invent remaps; never hardcode `:1234`/`:2346`. **Reuse** Glass: Read `$STYX_RUNTIME_DIR/sessions/<session_id>/glass-views.json` (else `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/styx-$UID/sessions/<session_id>/glass-views.json`) then `browser_navigate({ url, viewId })` — omit `position`; do not `newTab`. Do not wait for sessionStart “Known Glass views” (not model-visible). Prefer `submit_changes(wait_for_completion=false)` on stdio-bound sessions.

## Bootstrap

Notebook intent → **pluto-session** first. Glass: **`cursor-ide-browser`** (reuse with `viewId`; omit `position`; MCP ids are 6-hex — see **pluto-session** `glass-navigation.md`). Path B: after `open_notebook`, `browser_click` notebook on landing — not pasted `/edit?id=`. **Not** `plugin-browse-browser`. One window owns one Pluto; local Task children share that MCP. **Remote SSH:** stack on SSH host; local XOR remote; per-session Ports ask for Glass (`glass-navigation.md` / `remote-ssh.md`). Parent agents grading subagents: `eval/agent-control/`.

## Safe preview

Path B default = **Safe preview**. Still edit when asked. When outputs aren't live, **exit yourself** — Glass **Run notebook code** or MCP `allow_execution` — don't stop at staged edits with the gate still on. Detection → **pluto-workflow** `safe-preview.md`.

## Cell edits (notebook open)

Design Mode (**⌘⇧D**) → **`resolve_pluto_context`** → **`read_cell`** → stage → **`submit_changes(wait_for_completion=false)`** → exit Safe preview if needed → re-read.

Re-read before overwriting browser drafts. **`submit_changes(wait_for_completion=false)`** before ending turn if staged.
